IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-49. NOUNS of a cross-reference and of an amending instruction. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Securities Law, 5728-1968. It records two citations that name a section the Law no longer has, one citation that is sound and stands beside the second as a control,
-- and two amending instructions, one of which is the control for the first citation. For each citation it types what the citing words say they point at, what the target is, and where each of the two readings comes from.
-- A citation whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- Two of the kinds say, in their own words, that this row did not read the wording of the cited provision: the cited sections were repealed, and the text they had before the repeal is in none of the deposited pages.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the deposited excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation, whole-page line numbers;
-- `ext:[SH ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph (2) of subsection (ב) of section 35ד of the Law, whose wording this row did not read`
    `section 14א of the Law, whose wording this row did not read`
    `section 38 of the Law, the section on a court order`
    `a section of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text`

-- Four kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest.
-- The second kind is the honest name for a limb (a) whose repeal and commencement were read from the official pages while that nothing later brought the section back rests on the consolidation.
-- The third kind is the honest name for a limb (b) whose words were read from a page image of the enacting instrument while the place the words stand in and that nothing later changed them rest on the consolidation.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the same words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the official page image of the words as enacted; where those words stand and that no later instrument touched them are CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of an amending instruction`

DECLARE `An amending instruction` HAS
    `the instrument and section` IS A STRING
    `the schedule and item it changes` IS A STRING
    `it deletes the words naming section 35ד(ב)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instruction was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
